# Sample 3 - PSAssertedAccess manual requests
# Start sample:
#   dotnet run --project samples/PSAssertedAccess -- interactive

@resourceBase = https://localhost:3012
@psBase = https://localhost:3013
@apBase = https://localhost:3011
@agentJwt = {{$processEnv AGENT_JWT}}

### Metadata - Agent Provider
GET {{apBase}}/.well-known/aauth-agent.json

# VERIFY: 200 with jwks_uri and identifier

### Metadata - Resource
GET {{resourceBase}}/.well-known/aauth-resource.json

# VERIFY: 200 with resource identifier and capabilities

### Metadata - Person Server
GET {{psBase}}/.well-known/aauth-person.json

# VERIFY:
#   - 200 OK
#   - Body contains "token_endpoint" — where agents exchange resource tokens
#   - Body contains "jwks_uri" — PS's public keys for verifying auth tokens

### Step 1: POST /authorize (signed with agent token) -> resource_token
# dotnet run --project labs/scripts/AAuth.SignTool -- --jwt "$AGENT_JWT" --method POST --url "https://localhost:3012/authorize"
@authzSigKey = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_KEY
@authzSigInput = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_INPUT
@authzSig = REPLACE_SIGNATURE

POST {{resourceBase}}/authorize
Content-Type: application/json
Signature-Key: {{authzSigKey}}
Signature-Input: {{authzSigInput}}
Signature: {{authzSig}}

{
  "scope": "data.read"
}

# VERIFY:
#   - 200 OK
#   - Body JSON has "resource_token" — a JWT (typ: aa-resource+jwt)
#   - Decode the resource_token: aud=PS URL, agent=agent ID, scope=data.read
#   - The resource_token is an invitation for the PS to vouch for the agent

### Step 2: POST PS /token (signed with agent token) -> auth_token
@resourceToken = REPLACE_RESOURCE_TOKEN_JWT
# dotnet run --project labs/scripts/AAuth.SignTool -- --jwt "$AGENT_JWT" --method POST --url "https://localhost:3013/token"
@tokenSigKey = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_KEY
@tokenSigInput = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_INPUT
@tokenSig = REPLACE_SIGNATURE

POST {{psBase}}/token
Content-Type: application/json
Signature-Key: {{tokenSigKey}}
Signature-Input: {{tokenSigInput}}
Signature: {{tokenSig}}

{
  "resource_token": "{{resourceToken}}"
}

# VERIFY:
#   - 200 OK
#   - Body JSON has "auth_token" — a JWT (typ: aa-auth+jwt) issued by the PS
#   - Decode the auth_token: sub=person identity, aud=resource URL, agent=agent ID
#   - The auth_token's cnf.jwk matches the agent's ephemeral public key (PoP binding)

### Step 3: Access protected API with auth token (expected 200)
# ⚠️ RE-SIGN REQUIRED: Generate fresh headers.
# The auth token's cnf.jwk has only the PUBLIC key — you need the private key separately.
# Use `signing-key` command in the sample REPL to get the private key JWK, then:
@authToken = REPLACE_AUTH_TOKEN_JWT
# SIGNING_KEY=$(dotnet run --project samples/PSAssertedAccess -- <<< "signing-key" 2>/dev/null | grep '{')
# dotnet run --project labs/scripts/AAuth.SignTool -- --jwt "$authToken" --signing-key "$SIGNING_KEY" --method GET --url "https://localhost:3012/api/documents"
@accessSigKey = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_KEY
@accessSigInput = REPLACE_SIGNATURE_INPUT
@accessSig = REPLACE_SIGNATURE

GET {{resourceBase}}/api/documents
Signature-Key: {{accessSigKey}}
Signature-Input: {{accessSigInput}}
Signature: {{accessSig}}

# VERIFY:
#   - 200 OK with protected document data
#   - Note: Signature-Key contains the auth_token JWT (not the agent token)
#   - The resource verifies: auth token signature (PS issuer) + HTTP signature (agent's key)

### Step 4: Negative - call with agent token (expected 401 + AAuth-Requirement auth-token)
# ⚠️ RE-SIGN REQUIRED: Generate fresh signature headers using the agent token.
# The headers from step 1 have expired. Re-run the signing command from step 1.

GET {{resourceBase}}/api/documents
Signature-Key: {{authzSigKey}}
Signature-Input: {{authzSigInput}}
Signature: {{authzSig}}

# VERIFY:
#   - 401 Unauthorized
#   - "AAuth-Requirement" header: requirement=auth-token; resource-token="..."
#   - The resource_token inside the header is a fresh invitation for token exchange
#   - This proves: the resource requires an auth token (PS-asserted identity), not just any agent token
